  "notes": [
    "Partial encoding of Alaska Medicaid Nexletol / Nexlizet Criteria Version 1; Original 07/09/2020; Approval 09/18/2020; Effective 2020-11-16.",
    "Nexletol (bempedoic acid) and Nexlizet (bempedoic acid/ezetimibe) share identical criteria. ACL inhibitor; adjunct to diet and maximally tolerated statin therapy. No product-specific gate is needed.",
    "Closed indications require documented confirmed HeFH or established clinical ASCVD with at least one listed history. HeFH may coexist with ASCVD; LDL options attest actual ASCVD history rather than inferring absence from HeFH. The no-ASCVD LDL option is excluded for established ASCVD.",
    "LDL-C qualification: documented reduction <50% from baseline OR ASCVD with LDL-C >70 mg/dL OR no ASCVD history with LDL-C >100 mg/dL. Exactly 50%, 70 mg/dL or 100 mg/dL does not satisfy the corresponding strict threshold.",
    "Denial: failure to meet approval criteria, simvastatin >20 mg daily, pravastatin >40 mg daily, or current PCSK9 inhibitor use. Exactly 20 mg simvastatin and 40 mg pravastatin are allowed.",
    "Cautions (notes only): hyperuricemia has occurred; monitor serum uric acid as clinically indicated. Tendon rupture has occurred; discontinue at the first sign and avoid use in patients with previous tendon rupture.",
    "Duration (notes only): initial approval up to 3 months; reauthorization up to 12 months.",
    "Quantity (notes only): 30 tablets. max_units is null; quantity enforcement requires manual review.",
    "Remains partial: diagnosis, ASCVD history, specialist consultation, statin history, LDL response and concomitant drug doses are attestations. Evidence verification, cautions, duration, reauthorization and quantity require manual review. PDL status unknown."
  ],
  "max_units": null,
